# Token budget

This session is the control plane. Tokens die on retries, dumps, and re-reading history.

- Answer first. No recap of the last two days unless asked.
- Do not read agent transcripts or dump `git status` / build trees unless that is the task.
- One probe, then act. Same failure twice (agent `host disconnected`, SSH refused, port closed) → stop and tell the user. Do not poll 10–20 times.
- Never fetch or print device passwords from the VPS (sqlite, `get_password`, `device_passwords`). Use mesh SSH (`dustx-windows`) or already-open local APIs. If those are down, stop and say so.
- Prefer `ssh dustx-windows` when mesh is up. Do not start mesh unless SSH is needed this turn.
- Publish verify: hash + size + version from `/api/downloads/*` is enough. Do not GET the full zip unless hashes disagree.
- Commands: print only the lines that change the next step. No full cmake / certutil / tasklist dumps.
- Do not launch extra subagents, canvases, or parallel repo-wide greps for a single-host question.
